    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "\"As global populations increase, natural aggregate resources (sand, gravel, and stone) are needed to build and maintain the human system infrastructure.  Producing aggregate in an environmentally safe manner commonly requires environmental assessments. To minimize environmental damage, potential environmental impacts should be identified, characterized, and evaluated.  A hierarchical systems analysis (HSA) has been designed to characterize the environmental system components, identify potential impacts to those systems, and evaluate the extent of those impacts.\"",
